* Component Created by Javier Petrucci and Agustin Gullino
* jpetrucc@itba.edu.ar / agullino@itba.edu.ar
*
* This is the PNP BJT
*
*         C
*     |  /
*     | /
* B---|
*     | \
*     | _\|
*          E
*
*
*  /\Ic
*  |
*  |
*  |        /--------------------
*  |       /
*  |      /----------------------
*  |     /
*  |    /------------------------
*  |   /
*  |  /--------------------------
*  | /
*  |/__________________________________> Veb
*
*
* Behaviour:
*   - Veb = {Veb} at Ic = {Iref}, and it moves only n*60 mV per decade of
*     current (1.2 mV/decade with the default n = 0.02): an almost fixed Veb
*   - Ic = hfe * Ib exactly in the forward active region (no Early effect
*     unless {Va} is given)
*   - the knee is sharp: the BC junction has its own ideality {ns}, so the
*     whole transition happens within a few mV of {Vsat}
*   - in saturation Vec sits at about {Vsat}
*   - not meant for the reverse active region: the reverse channel exists
*     only so the transistor saturates (see below)
*   - cutoff is clean: the junctions leak about 1e-18 A
*
* The model is the Ebers-Moll transport model, the same structure as the
* Gummel-Poon BJT of SPICE with only its ideal part:
*   - two exponential junction diodes (EB and CB) whose currents are the
*     forward and reverse base currents
*   - two LINEAR current-controlled current sources that carry hfe times the
*     forward base current from collector to emitter and br times the
*     reverse base current back
* Saturation is not imposed by any switching factor: when Vec falls under
* {Vsat} the CB junction turns on and its transport term cancels the forward
* one, as in a real transistor. The CB junction is shifted so that it
* reaches the same current at Veb-{Vsat} that the EB junction carries at
* {Veb}; that is what puts the knee at {Vsat}.
*
* Convergence notes (why this replaces the previous version):
*   - the previous model used LTspice ideal diodes (Ron/Roff/Vfwd), which
*     ngspice does not have and get translated to piecewise-linear sources,
*     and a behavioural source hfe*I(Vf)*tanh(...). Its Jacobian had a slope
*     of hfe/Ron = 1e4 S and kinks at every corner, so Newton overshot and
*     needed gmin or source stepping, and often failed.
*   - here the only nonlinear elements are two ordinary ngspice diodes, which
*     have junction voltage limiting (pnjlim) built for exactly this
*     exponential, and everything else is linear. Operating point,
*     transient and AC converge on the direct Newton iteration.
*   - a small n makes Veb flat but the junction steep. ngspice clamps the
*     diode IS to 1e-28 and the BJT limiter ignores NF, so the junction uses
*     a normal IS and the zero volt ammeters Vf/Vr become fixed offsets that
*     place the knee at {Veb}. Values of n from 0.02 to 1 converge; 1 is a
*     real silicon junction, 0.02 an almost ideal one.
*   - the reverse beta br is not a parameter. It is fixed internally to
*     br = min(1, 0.5*(Veb/Vsat-1)), which keeps
*     (1+br)*{Vsat} < {Veb}: the device is passive for any {Vsat} < {Veb}.
*
* Small signal (AC): gm = Ic/(n*Vt) and r_pi = hfe/gm, as in a real
* transistor but with n making it n times smaller. {cje} and {cjc} are
* fixed junction capacitances and {tf} the forward transit time (diffusion
* capacitance tf*gm), so fT = 1/(2*pi*tf) when tf dominates.
*
* Parameters:
*   hfe    forward beta                                   100
*   Veb    Veb at Ic = Iref                                0.7
*   Vsat   Vec at the saturation knee                       0.3
*   Iref   current at which Veb is exact                    1m
*   n      junction ideality (0.02 ideal, 1 silicon)     0.02
*   ns     ideality of the BC junction: sets how sharp the
*          saturation knee is (10-90 % in ~2 mV at 0.01)   0.01
*   Va     Early voltage (0 = no Early effect)            0
*   cje, cjc  junction capacitances                       2p, 1p
*   tf     forward transit time                           0

.SUBCKT PNP_nice C B E PARAMS: hfe=100 Veb=0.7 Vsat=0.3 Iref=1m n=0.02 ns=0.01 Va=0 cje=2p cjc=1p tf=0
.param vt0=0.025852 isd=1e-18
.param br={min(1, 0.5*(Veb/Vsat-1))}
.param ga={Va > 0 ? 1/Va : 0}
.param vof={Veb-n*vt0*ln(Iref/hfe/isd)}
.param vor={Veb-Vsat-ns*vt0*ln(Iref/br/isd)}

**Emitter base junction. Vf measures the forward base current
Vf  Nf B  {vof}
Deb E  Nf DJF
**Collector base junction. Vr measures the reverse base current
Vr  Nr B  {vor}
Dcb C  Nr DJR

**Transport: forward and reverse channels, linear in the base currents
F1  E  C  Vf {hfe}
F2  C  E  Vr {br}
**Early effect: output conductance Ic/Va, only when Va > 0
Bea E  C  I = {hfe*ga}*I(Vf)*V(E,C)

**Junction capacitances and diffusion capacitance
Ceb E  B  {cje}
Ccb C  B  {cjc}

.model DJF D(IS={isd} N={n} TT={tf*hfe})
.model DJR D(IS={isd} N={ns} TT={tf*br})

.ends PNP_nice
